This solution uses a backtracking algorithm to generate all possible permutations of the given array of distinct integers. The `backtrack` method is a recursive helper function that builds permutations by adding one element at a time and ensuring that no duplicates are included. The `main` method includes test cases to verify the correctness of the `permute` function.

